    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n### 1. **Governance module** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n- **Problem**: The test tried to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it wasn't being exported from the module.\n- **Solution**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` at the top level of the module, while keeping them in the default export as well.\n\n### 2. **Evaluation module** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\n- **Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function was defined with signature `(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)`, but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`. This caused references to be misinterpreted as banned terms, incorrectly flagging valid output as toxic.\n- **Solution**: Changed the signature to `(outputs, references = null)` and always use `defaultBannedTerms`, matching the calling convention expected by `runEvaluations`.\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files  \n\u2705 All existing public exports remain intact",
